    "result_text": "I've traced the full picture. Here's what I found:\n\n**The change is already fully implemented and all tests pass.** Let me summarize the verification:\n\nAll three rejection status codes (400, 409, 429) are produced exclusively through `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, and every handler routes through a single `detailBuild(...)` helper that constructs a Spring `ProblemDetail`:\n\n- **400 Bad Request** \u2014 `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException` (Bean Validation) and `handleFieldValidationException` (`RequiredFieldsMissingException` / `InvalidFieldsException`)\n- **409 Conflict** \u2014 `handleDuplicateIdentityException`, `handleCityCapacityExceededException`\n- **429 Too Many Requests** \u2014 `handleDailyOwnerLimitExceededException`\n\n`detailBuild` (`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java:67`) sets all four required RFC7807 members:\n- `type` \u2192 request URL (a URI)\n- `title` \u2192 exception class simple name\n- `status` \u2192 the HTTP status (inherent to `ProblemDetail.forStatus`)\n- `detail` \u2192 the human-readable message\n\nEach handler returns `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>`, which Spring serializes with `Content-Type: application/problem+json` (HTTP codes unchanged). The dead `BindingErrorsResponse` class is no longer wired into any validation path, so there's no competing non-problem+json 400 route.\n\nThe acceptance test confirms this end-to-end:\n\n```\nTests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0\nBUILD SUCCESS\n```\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` exercises a real 400 (owner with missing `city`) and asserts both `content().contentTypeCompatibleWith(\"application/problem+json\")` and `jsonPath(\"$.status\").value(400)` \u2014 both pass. Since 409 and 429 share the identical `ProblemDetail`/`ResponseEntity` code path, they produce the same problem+json shape.\n\nI made no code edits because the specification was already satisfied and the suite was green \u2014 fabricating changes would only risk regressing a correct implementation. The task is complete and verified.",
